    "problem_statement": "QR code data encoding produces incorrect output\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes with certain data, the encoded output appears to be corrupted or incorrect. The QR code generation process seems to be reversing or manipulating the input data in unexpected ways.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\n# Create a QR code with alphanumeric data\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(version=1)\nqr.add_data('HELLO123')\nqr.make()\n\n# The generated QR code doesn't encode the expected data\n# When scanned, it shows garbled or incorrect content\n```\n\nAlso happens with numeric data:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(version=1)\nqr.add_data('12345')\nqr.make()\n\n# The numeric encoding appears to be corrupted\n```\n\nThe issue seems to affect all data modes (numeric, alphanumeric, and byte mode). When you scan the generated QR codes, they don't contain the original input data as expected."
